    "feasibility_not_success": "a non-negative slack only means the adaptive-margin hinge can be zero at the teacher optimum; it is NOT evidence that retraining will succeed and a non-zero initial gradient is NOT accuracy",
    "js_skl_inequality": "JS(p,q) = 0.5 KL(p||m) + 0.5 KL(q||m) with m=(p+q)/2; convexity of KL in its second argument gives KL(p||m) <= 0.5 KL(p||q) and KL(q||m) <= 0.5 KL(q||p), hence JS <= 0.5(KL(p||q)+KL(q||p)) = symmetric_KL and the adaptive-margin slack D_swap - JS is non-negative at the teacher optimum.",
